theory('Bit PreRequisites for TRIE Problems', 'A binary trie follows one edge per bit, from bit 31 down to 0. Extract via `(x >>> bit) & 1`, which works with signed patterns. To maximize XOR, prefer the opposite bit when a matching stored prefix exists. Greedy works because the highest differing bit contributes more than every lower bit combined. Define signed versus unsigned optimization explicitly: these lessons restrict numbers to nonnegative ints, so signed and unsigned ordering agree. Offline bound queries sort by bound and insert only eligible values before querying.')
trie = '''    static class Node { Node[] child=new Node[26]; int pass,end; }
    static class Trie {
        final Node root=new Node();
        private int index(char c){ if(c<'a'||c>'z') throw new IllegalArgumentException("lowercase only"); return c-'a'; }
        void insert(String word){ for(char c:word.toCharArray()) index(c); Node p=root; p.pass++; for(char c:word.toCharArray()){ int i=index(c); if(p.child[i]==null) p.child[i]=new Node(); p=p.child[i]; p.pass++; } p.end++; }
        Node walk(String s){ Node p=root; for(char c:s.toCharArray()){ p=p.child[index(c)]; if(p==null) return null; } return p; }
        boolean search(String word){ Node p=walk(word); return p!=null&&p.end>0; }
        boolean startsWith(String prefix){ Node p=walk(prefix); return p!=null&&p.pass>0; }
        int countWordsEqualTo(String word){ Node p=walk(word); return p==null?0:p.end; }
        int countWordsStartingWith(String prefix){ Node p=walk(prefix); return p==null?0:p.pass; }
        boolean erase(String word){ if(!search(word)) return false; Node p=root; p.pass--; for(char c:word.toCharArray()){ p=p.child[index(c)]; p.pass--; } p.end--; return true; }
    }'''
for title,advanced in [('Trie Implementation and Operations',False),('Trie Implementation and Advanced Operations',True)]:
    add(title,trie, 'Trie t=new Trie(); t.insert("apple"); t.insert("apple"); System.out.println(t.search("apple")); System.out.println(t.startsWith("app"));'+ (' t.erase("apple"); System.out.println(t.countWordsEqualTo("apple"));' if advanced else ''),
        'true\ntrue\n1' if advanced else 'true\ntrue',
        'Lowercase trie supporting insert, exact search and prefix search. Advanced variant additionally counts duplicate words and erases one occurrence safely.',
        'Every root-to-node path represents one prefix. pass counts inserted word occurrences traversing the node; end counts exact word occurrences. Erase first confirms existence so counters cannot underflow.',
        'O(word length) time per operation; O(total distinct-prefix nodes*26) storage. Erase retains allocated nodes, so memory tracks historical prefixes.',
        'Two insertions of apple make its end count 2; deleting once changes it to 1 while app remains a live prefix.',
        'Search is not the same as prefix existence: app is a prefix but not a complete word unless inserted. Empty strings are supported at root. Character validation occurs before insert mutates counters.')
add('Longest Word with All Prefixes',trie+'''\n    public static String solve(String[] words){ Trie t=new Trie(); for(String w:words) t.insert(w); String best=""; for(String w:words){ Node p=t.root; boolean valid=true; for(char c:w.toCharArray()){ p=p.child[c-'a']; if(p.end==0){ valid=false; break; } } if(valid&&(w.length()>best.length()||w.length()==best.length()&&w.compareTo(best)<0)) best=w; } return best; }''','System.out.println(solve(new String[]{"n","ni","nin","ninj","ninja","ninga"}));','ninja',
    'Return longest lowercase word whose every nonempty prefix is also in the dictionary; ties are lexicographic. Return empty if absent.', 'Insert all words, then walk each word checking end>0 at every prefix node. This directly tests the contract.', 'O(total word characters) time; O(total trie nodes*26) space.', 'n,ni,nin,ninj,ninja all exist; ninga fails at ning.', 'A trie path existing does not imply it is a complete inserted prefix; check end counters.')
add('Number of distinct substrings in a string', '''    static class Node { Node[] child=new Node[26]; }
    public static long solve(String s){ for(char c:s.toCharArray()) if(c<'a'||c>'z') throw new IllegalArgumentException(); Node root=new Node(); long count=1; for(int start=0;start<s.length();start++){ Node p=root; for(int end=start;end<s.length();end++){ int x=s.charAt(end)-'a'; if(p.child[x]==null){ p.child[x]=new Node(); count++; } p=p.child[x]; } } return count; }''','System.out.println(solve("ababa"));','10',
    'Count DISTINCT substring values, INCLUDING the empty substring, for lowercase input.', 'Insert every suffix into a trie. Every nonroot node represents one unique nonempty substring as its root path; count only newly created nodes and add one for empty.', 'O(n²) time, O(26*n²) worst trie space.', 'ababa has 9 distinct nonempty substrings; adding empty gives 10.', 'Many judges exclude empty; return count-1 for that variant. This counts distinct values, not n*(n+1)/2 occurrences.', 'Suffix automata can count distinct substrings in O(n) states/time for fixed alphabet, but require a different construction.')
binary_trie = '''    static class BitNode { BitNode[] child=new BitNode[2]; }
    static void insert(BitNode root,int x){ if(x<0) throw new IllegalArgumentException(); BitNode p=root; for(int bit=30;bit>=0;bit--){ int b=(x>>>bit)&1; if(p.child[b]==null) p.child[b]=new BitNode(); p=p.child[b]; } }
    static int query(BitNode root,int x){ if(x<0) throw new IllegalArgumentException(); int ans=0; BitNode p=root; for(int bit=30;bit>=0;bit--){ int b=(x>>>bit)&1; if(p.child[1-b]!=null){ ans|=1<<bit; p=p.child[1-b]; } else p=p.child[b]; } return ans; }'''
add('Maximum XOR of two numbers in an array',binary_trie+'''\n    public static int solve(int[] a){ if(a.length<2) return 0; BitNode root=new BitNode(); insert(root,a[0]); int best=0; for(int i=1;i<a.length;i++){ best=Math.max(best,query(root,a[i])); insert(root,a[i]); } return best; }''','System.out.println(solve(new int[]{3,10,5,25,2,8}));','28',
    'For nonnegative ints find maximum XOR from two distinct array positions. Fewer than two entries returns zero.', 'Store earlier numbers in a binary trie. At each high-to-low bit prefer the opposite branch; the highest gained bit outweighs every possible loss below it. Query before inserting current to enforce distinct indices.', 'O(31*n) time/space; 31 is a fixed-width bound.', '5 XOR 25 = 28, binary 11100.', 'This trie optimizes nonnegative int XOR; arbitrary signed maximum requires a sign-bit-aware ordering contract.', 'Pair enumeration takes O(n²) time and O(1) space.')
add('Maximum Xor with an element from an array',binary_trie+'''\n    public static int[] solve(int[] input,int[][] queries){ int[] a=input.clone(); Arrays.sort(a); Integer[] order=new Integer[queries.length]; for(int i=0;i<order.length;i++) order[i]=i; Arrays.sort(order,(i,j)->Integer.compare(queries[i][1],queries[j][1])); int[] out=new int[queries.length]; BitNode root=new BitNode(); int at=0; for(int i:order){ int x=queries[i][0],limit=queries[i][1]; while(at<a.length&&a[at]<=limit) insert(root,a[at++]); out[i]=at==0?-1:query(root,x); } return out; }''','System.out.println(Arrays.toString(solve(new int[]{0,1,2,3,4},new int[][]{{3,1},{1,3},{5,6}})));','[3, 3, 7]',
    'Each query [x,limit] asks max x XOR value for an array value <=limit, with nonnegative values/x. Return -1 if none.', 'Sort array and queries by limit. Insert each newly eligible value once, then query the trie. Restore original query order by storing its index.', 'O(n log n+q log q+31*(n+q)) time; O(31*n+q+n) space.', 'For [3,1] eligible values 0,1 give max 3; for [5,6] all values eligible and 5^2=7.', 'Query sorting must retain original indices. Bound may be negative, yielding no eligible nonnegative values.')
